                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't know why  there is so few review of this game yet, because it's a really good quality picross game! \n\nWhat I like about the game:\n+3 difficulty mode. You can either solve it as 1 big picross or solve it by color\n+Stars you get on puzzle completion are not difficulty dependent\n+Color theme of UI/puzzle is really gorgeous! ♥\n+Row and colum highlight is same color as current color (nice touch)\n+You can cancel sliding mouse click by going diagonaly\n+Tile sound (when painting) is not too loud\n+Auto-cross the empty tiles when all hints are found (depending on difficulty it changes a little)\n+Count tiles when slide\n+You can change the color of the tile AND the color of the background\n\nA little bit of negative nitpicking:\n (not really relevant to picross solving)\n-I think that some of the UI buttons are bouncing a bit too much\n-I don't like the real fireplace. I think a cartonny fire would have fit better\n-i don't really like the skip button. I think that the goal of the game is to discover the image. I would have remove this option since there is already tons of abilities and mode to help you solve puzzles\n-I would have wrote proper description in upgrade menu hover like \"Add 1 heart\", \"Range of ability increase by 1\" instead of \"Upgrade bonus\"\n-Tile animation when loading a puzzle is a little bit long\n-Escape keyboard button doesn't bring menu. It would be easy to add this functionnality.\n-Price is way to low for all the great unique puzzle you can solve! I would have sold it between 6 to 9 US $ without hesitation\n\nI am not shy to say that this is the best colored oriented picross game currently on steam! The quality of the UI, the color of the puzzle, the power system that help you solve puzzle is just very well implemented! The game flow without resistance making you want to play for hours to discover all puzzles!\n\nI appreciate the dev team that brought this game into the world and wish you the best for your next game ♥",
                        "timestamp_created": 1558819430,
